From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: modifiers only from input events

Every event that reaches handleEvent re-reads the modifier flags and
releases the guest's modifiers that are not set. The pointer entering or
leaving a window comes as an event without flags, so crossing from one
window to another released a held key: with a window per display, Super
went up halfway through a Super-drag of a guest window to the other display
and Hyprland dropped the move. Only key, mouse button, move, drag, scroll and
pinch events carry the modifier state; other events are not looked at.

Upstream: upstreamable (upstream has the same sync; with one window it only
shows when the pointer re-enters with a modifier held).
Test: Cmd-drag of a guest window from the external display to the MacBook
and back, 6 of 6 moved (before: 0, Super released at the display edge).
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-fullscreen-size.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -1216,6 +1216,32 @@
     InputButton button;
     unsigned int keycode;
     NSUInteger modifiers = [event modifierFlags];
+
+    /*
+     * OmacVM: only input events tell the modifier state. The pointer entering
+     * or leaving a window comes with no flags at all, and would release a
+     * held modifier: Super halfway through a Super-drag to another display.
+     */
+    switch ([event type]) {
+    case NSEventTypeKeyDown:
+    case NSEventTypeKeyUp:
+    case NSEventTypeFlagsChanged:
+    case NSEventTypeLeftMouseDown:
+    case NSEventTypeLeftMouseUp:
+    case NSEventTypeLeftMouseDragged:
+    case NSEventTypeRightMouseDown:
+    case NSEventTypeRightMouseUp:
+    case NSEventTypeRightMouseDragged:
+    case NSEventTypeOtherMouseDown:
+    case NSEventTypeOtherMouseUp:
+    case NSEventTypeOtherMouseDragged:
+    case NSEventTypeMouseMoved:
+    case NSEventTypeScrollWheel:
+    case NSEventTypeMagnify:
+        break;
+    default:
+        return false;
+    }
 
     /*
      * Check -[NSEvent modifierFlags] here.
